  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed in both technical and everyday contexts. The compound {発光|はっこう}ダイオード (LED — light-emitting diode) is one of the most common collocations.\n\nBe careful not to confuse this word with other はっこう homophones: {発行|はっこう} (publication/issuance), {発効|はっこう} (taking effect), and {発酵|はっこう} (fermentation).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {発光|はっこう}ダイオード (light-emitting diode / LED)\n- {発光|はっこう}する{生物|せいぶつ} (bioluminescent organism)\n- {発光|はっこう}{体|たい} (luminous body)\n- {蛍光|けいこう}{発光|はっこう} (fluorescent emission)",
